UID:1788c837d1cf5798@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261009T223613Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261009
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Saving Money on Winter Heating Costs
DESCRIPTION:Hello\, this is Governor Janet Mills\, and thank you for liste
 ning.\nWell\, it's getting more and more painful to fill up at a gas stati
 on or fill a tank of oil to heat your home. And we all know why.\nLook\, w
 e're making progress shifting to other sources of energy to heat our homes
 \, but we're still the most dependent on heating oil to heat our homes in 
 the in the entire country. That reliance on heating oil makes us vulnerabl
 e to great shifts in global energy markets that drive up costs for Maine p
 eople and businesses. This president's war in Iran right now has created t
 he largest fuel supply disruption in global history and has driven energy 
 prices to record highs. The price of heating oil in Maine has reached more
  than $6 a gallon\, so you'll be paying almost $800 more to fill a standar
 d 275 gallon tank than you did a year ago. Kerosene prices are also reachi
 ng historic highs\, all because of this war.\nMaine people should not be f
 orced to choose between staying warm or putting food on the table because 
 the president chose to drag us into a needless war -- and an endless war\,
  it appears.\nMy administration is doing what it can to help people save m
 oney on heating costs and stay comfortable in their homes this winter.\nIt
 's not enough\, but I've directed the Department of Health and Human Servi
 ces to identify households that would be eligible for $40 million in disco
 unts on their electric bills through Maine's Low Income Assistance Program
 \, or LIAP. Starting in November\, thousands of eligible families who are 
 customers of CMP or Versant will begin to see discounts ranging from 20 pe
 rcent to 80 percent\, and these will be applied automatically every month 
 to their electric bills. It's one thing we can do. Families who already ge
 t federal assistance for home heating oil through LIHEAP\, the Low Income 
 Energy Assistance Program\, will also be enrolled automatically in this st
 ate assistance program\, LIAP\, to get the maximum savings on their electr
 ic bills without any unnecessary pa\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/n
 ews/radio_address/saving-money-winter-heating-costs-2026-10-09
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/news/radio_address/saving-money-wi
 nter-heating-costs-2026-10-09
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:86e120e3d258eaae@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261009T223525Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261009
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] 10/9/2026: Maine eCourts Scheduled to be Impl
 emented in  Lincoln\, Knox\, Sagadahoc\, and Waldo Courts in December
DESCRIPTION:Home\nSkip to top navigation\nSkip to side navigation\nSkip to
  content\nSkip to footer\nMaine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp
 \n|\nSearch Maine.gov\nCOURT ALERTS IN EFFECT.\nSee Active Alerts\nHome\n
 →\nNews & Announcements\nMaine eCourts Scheduled to be Implemented in  L
 incoln\, Knox\, Sagadahoc\, and Waldo Courts in December\nDate:\n10/9/2026
 \nThe Maine Judicial Branch announced today that District and Superior Cou
 rts in Lincoln\, Knox\, Sagadahoc\, and Waldo counties (comprising Judicia
 l Region 6) will transition from paper filing to electronic filing (eFilin
 g) on Monday\, December 7\, 2026. All case types in the Lincoln\, Knox\, S
 agadahoc and Waldo County Unified Criminal Dockets (UCDs) and Superior Cou
 rts\; and in the Belfast\, Rockland\, West Bath\, and Wiscasset District C
 ourts will transition to eFiling. To help attorneys and other stakeholders
  in Region 6 get ready for eFiling\, the Judicial Branch will hold a virtu
 al presentation by Zoom:\nTopic: Maine eCourts in Region 6: Lincoln\, Knox
 \, Sagadahoc and Waldo County\nDate & Time: Wednesday\, October 14\, 2026 
 at 12:00 p.m.\nPlease click the link below to join the webinar:\nhttps://c
 ourts-maine-gov.zoom.us/j/96415858276\nPasscode: 522889\nThe Zoom presenta
 tion will be recorded and posted on the Maine eCourts Training & Resources
  page following the live session.\neFiler Trainings for Attorneys and Staf
 f\nMembers of the Maine eCourts project team will conduct in-person traini
 ng for attorneys and staff according to the schedule below. Please note\, 
 registration is required to attend a training session. Prosecutors and sta
 ff will receive a separate link to register by email.\nProsecutor eFiler T
 raining - Thursday\, November 5th from 9:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m. (Knox County
  Superior Court\, Rockland) Registration link to be sent by email\nAll Oth
 er eFiler Training  Monday\, November 2nd from 1:00 p.m. to 4:00 p.m. (Kno
 x County Superior Court\, Rockland) Register for this session\nRegion 6 Wi
 ll Be the Second to Last Judicial Region to Complete the Transition to eF\
 nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13363819
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13363819
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
